# COMPILED BYTECODE MUST NEVER BE COMMITTED.
#
# On 17.9.2026 a `git add -A` swept __pycache__/engine.cpython-312.pyc into
# the repository, and the deployed app then failed with an ImportError on
# `from engine import run_transcription` — a name that is plainly there in
# the source.
#
# A .pyc carries the Python version in its name and a magic number inside
# it. Whether it is used, ignored, or shadows the source depends on which
# Python the server happens to run, which is not something a repository
# should ever leave to chance.
#
# It is also the exact trap written into MANTRA_MANIFEST as
# checking-the-checks.md face 7: stale bytecode gives results that exist
# nowhere in the source.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Never a secret, never a key file.
.streamlit/secrets.toml
*.key
